---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SurveySamples from '../components/SurveySamples.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_TEL } from '../lib/site.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Foundation Repair Advocate — Arizona second opinions & floor surveys"
  description="Paid independent foundation second opinions and floor elevation surveys in Arizona. Complete the picture before you sign a repair contract. White Mountains, Show Low, and statewide."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">A voice of reason.</p>
      <h1>You have options they didn't mention.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        Independent floor elevation surveys and foundation second opinions for Arizona homeowners.
        We exist to give you the full picture before you sign a repair contract — including when
        monitoring, drainage, or a deeper engineering look is the wiser first move.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>Call {PHONE}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works/">How it works</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-note">
        A paid decision tool before you sign a repair contract: measured documentation and an
        independent practical opinion. We do not diagnose structural adequacy, design repairs, or
        provide stamped engineering. Not a free sales inspection, not a pier company, not a full
        geotech package — clarity, including when the honest answer is
        <em>wait and monitor</em>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="hero-visual">
      <img
        src="/images/sample-settlement.jpg"
        alt="Sample floor elevation survey map showing a contour map of a home's floor with a low point marked near the perimeter"
        width={1488}
        height={1162}
        loading="eager"
      />
      <figcaption>
        A sample floor elevation survey — <a href="#survey-samples-heading">see how to read one ↓</a>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="container-wide">
    <section>
      <h2>What most homeowners never hear</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Foundation problems rarely come with one answer. Monitor. Fix drainage first. Repair part of
        the house. Wait a year and measure again. Act now. Free proposal visits often lead with the
        repair path; other paths get less time. Some homes need piers or other repair — and when the
        evidence supports that, we say so. We're independent of repair, not opposed to it. You pay so
        every credible option gets a fair hearing.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>You can absolutely fix it — you don't have to right now.</strong> That sentence
          rarely gets said in a living room. When repair <em>is</em> the right answer — including
          piers — we say so, and help you ask better questions of the people who do the work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <div class="card-grid three">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Floor elevation survey</h3>
          <p>
            A careful survey of the living floors using a water manometer — typically more accepted
            because the readings are repeatable over time. Contour map of highs and lows, and a
            plain-language read of what the pattern suggests before a high-cost decision.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Second opinion on bids</h3>
          <p>
            Already have a survey or a scary estimate? We review pier count, methods, and language
            against measured data — and surface the questions that often don't get asked.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Monitor &amp; resurvey</h3>
          <p>
            When movement is real but not urgent, we document a baseline and what to watch for over
            the next year — then compare again if needed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        We provide measured documentation and an independent practical opinion — experience and
        forensic observation, not a full geotechnical or structural investigation. Those go deeper
        (and cost more) when the facts call for them.
        <a href="/disclosure/">Read the full scope →</a>
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
        <a href="/what-you-get/">See everything included →</a>
        &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/guides/">Read the guides →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <SurveySamples />

    <section>
      <h2>Who this is for</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>You got a foundation repair estimate and something feels off</li>
        <li>You want independent measurement before you commit to a large repair</li>
        <li>You already paid for a floor survey from a repair company and want an independent read</li>
        <li>You're in Show Low, the White Mountains, or anywhere in Arizona and want a straight answer</li>
        <li>
          You're a realtor or party to a transaction and need a calm, paid measurement step — not
          another sales visit
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Ready when you are</h2>
      <p>
        Call before you sign a repair contract. Surveys are scheduled by phone; we'll walk you
        through a simple floor-plan scan before your visit so we're ready to measure when we arrive.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>Call or text {PHONE}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
